  "week_in_review": {
    "text": "The week's data bears mainly on the flood question. New CVE records for the 13 weeks to 14 Nov stand at 46,292, 5.4 times the 2023–24 pace. On exploitation, the median from disclosure to CISA listing was 15.5 days over 26 weeks, against 21 in 2023–24, while the share already exploited at disclosure showed no clear change. Several incidents ran through supply links rather than new flaws: a stolen key at an AI-tool marketplace, a legacy system at a shipper, a Taiwanese e-commerce platform. Whether organisations patch more quickly is not publicly measurable day to day.",
    "strongest_against": {
      "text": "The FAA's nationwide ground stop was blamed on a routine equipment upgrade, and its administrator said there was zero evidence of anything AI-related, per TechCrunch.",
